{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790967646,"nonce":"hk5iyTdpMlkX20bLhBBKMOyILiw=","title":"No first-party `blinc dev`: hot reload still needs dx serve","message":"Hot patching works, but the dev-server half is Dioxus's. A user has to\ninstall `dx` and run `dx serve --hot-patch`; Blinc supplies only the\nin-process patch points and the websocket client that talks to it.\nBlinc apps do not link the Dioxus reactive runtime at runtime — just\n`subsecond`, `tungstenite` and the env-var convention crate.\n\nVendoring the dev-server side makes `blinc dev` a first-party command\nwith no `dx` install, and opens up tightening rebuild detection to\nBlinc's own tree: invalidating `Stylesheet` caches when a CSS-only file\nchanges, for one.\n\nWas \"level 2\" in the hot-reload chapter's roadmap section.","files":null}]}